## At a glance

| Dimension | OpenObserve | Tracify |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Model** | Open source + cloud | SaaS only |
| **Primary focus** | Logs, metrics, traces (all) | LLM tracing + evaluation |
| **LLM-specific** | No | Yes |
| **Evaluation** | No (external tools) | Integrated |
| **Cost tracking** | None | Native |
| **Self-hosted** | Yes | No |
| **Best for** | Infrastructure teams | LLM/agent teams |

OpenObserve is a generalist observability platform; Tracify is specialized for LLMs and agents.

## Core difference

**OpenObserve** is infrastructure-first: logs, metrics, traces in one platform. **Tracify** is LLM-first: traces + evaluation + cost, optimized for agents.

Choose OpenObserve for infrastructure observability; choose Tracify for LLM observability.

## Scenario 1: infrastructure and LLM observability together

You want one platform for infrastructure (logs, metrics) and LLMs (traces, evaluation).

**With OpenObserve:** Logs and metrics are native. LLM tracing requires custom instrumentation.

**With Tracify + existing platform:** Keep OpenObserve for infrastructure. Add Tracify for LLM-specific signals.

**Result:** Complementary, not competing.

## Scenario 2: LLM observability only

You don't need infrastructure observability, just LLM traces and evaluation.

**With OpenObserve:** Generic trace storage. Evaluation and cost tracking require external tools.

**With Tracify:** Traces, evaluation, cost tracking all included.

**Result:** Tracify is simpler for LLM-only workloads.

## Cost and setup

**OpenObserve:** Self-hosted (free software, your infrastructure) or cloud ($300-500/month)
**Tracify:** $1,000+/month SaaS

If you self-host OpenObserve, cost is lower but operational burden is higher.

## When to choose each

**Choose OpenObserve:** If you need infrastructure + LLM observability, and self-hosting works for you
**Choose Tracify:** If you want LLM-specific features (evaluation, cost tracking) without infrastructure overhead

## FAQ

{% faq-item question="Can I use both?" answer="Yes. OpenObserve for infrastructure, Tracify for LLM signals." /%}

{% faq-item question="Does OpenObserve have evaluation?" answer="No, OpenObserve requires external tools." /%}

{% faq-item question="Is self-hosting OpenObserve cheaper?" answer="Cheaper at scale, but higher operational burden." /%}

{% faq-item question="Which is better for production?" answer="OpenObserve for infrastructure-heavy systems; Tracify for LLM-heavy systems." /%}

{% faq-item question="Can OpenObserve replace Tracify?" answer="Only if you build evaluation and cost tracking yourself." /%}
